# The vision interpreter's direct requirements (Python 3.11, Linux x86_64): the models' stack,
# the dependencies of packages/core and the test tools. requirements-gpu.txt is the hashed lock
# made from this file (see README.md in this directory); edit this file, then compile again.
# Our own code is not installed there: packages/core/src and packages/vision/src go on
# PYTHONPATH. Not in uv.lock: the agent venv never installs torch.

# The models. PyPI's torch 2.14.0 Linux wheels are built for CUDA 13.0 and pull the nvidia-*-cu13
# runtime wheels; the driver must support CUDA 13 (driver 580 or newer).
